  "discussion": "No big updates are expected this morning with surf numbers staying on track. A small, medium-period north (010 degrees) swell will continue to decline today. Surf along north and west-facing shores will decline somewhat this morning, then hold steady with the arrival of a new small, north- northwest swell that peaks this afternoon and evening. Surf will continue to decline on Thursday as the new swell fades. Another small north-northwest swell is forecast to arrive and build on Saturday, peaking Saturday night into Sunday, with a larger swell possible next Tuesday. Rough surf along east-facing shores will hold near seasonal averages today into Thursday. A slight increase in east shore surf is expected Friday and Saturday as trade winds strengthen. Mainly small background level surf is expected along south-facing shores during the next several days. A small bump is possible this afternoon for south-facing shores with a medium-period swell. Another small, long- period swell brings a bump to south shore surf on Friday.",
